        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e65aa564-ebaa-53aa-a9ee-4c61f91e9d48",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Chelidonium majus, Duranta, Stylophorum diphyllum\n- Taxonomy: Chelidonium, Verbenaceae\n- Common names: greater celandine, tetterwort, nipplewort, swallowwort\n\nFacts:\n- Chelidonium majus is commonly known as greater celandine, tetterwort, nipplewort, or swallowwort, although tetterwort also refers to Sanguinaria canadensis.\n- Chelidonium majus is a herbaceous perennial plant and the only species in the genus Chelidonium.\n- Duranta is a genus of flowering plants in the verbena family, Verbenaceae.\n- The common name of Stylophorum diphyllum is derived from greater celandine, Chelidonium majus, a closely related European plant with similarly shaped leaves and similarly coloured and shaped flowers.",
